{"id":"graph-view","parent":"sd-nav","ord":"a0","title":"Graph view: the reference graph as a navigable map","todo":true,"desc":"- `/graph/<id>` shows a node's neighbourhood; `/graph` the whole reference graph. Click to navigate; files drawn as groupings.\n- PR #247 built it but is parked as a draft: the human found it unsatisfying because .md documents aren't in the graph, and bolting that on would be messy.\n- Waits on the nodes/documents unification design (brainstorming/first-class-documents.md); rebuild on addresses once that lands.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:44-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#247 parked as draft 2026-08-19 — the human ruled it unsatisfying: no .md/.olai parity, and bolting parity on would make a ball of mud; waits on the nodes/docs unification architecture (brainstorming doc)","unblocked-by":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — rebuilt on addresses at step 4 of its path"}}
{"id":"search-document-bodies","parent":"sd-search","ord":"a0","title":"Search inside HTML documents — needs a ruling first #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- Search already covers markdown document bodies (shipped with #258).\n- What's left: `.html` files. Their text isn't searchable because the server deliberately doesn't keep HTML bodies in memory (they can be megabytes).\n- Needs a decision before any code: either declare HTML opaque to search and close this, or design an index that reads bodies at search time without loading them all.\n- Related: the parked semantic-recall work.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:44-04:00"}
{"id":"md-live-preview-editor","parent":"sd-docs","ord":"a0","title":"Markdown editing gets live preview (parked — draft PR #241)","doing":true,"desc":"- Parked 2026-08-18 by the human (\"revisit in distant future\"); draft PR #241 holds the work, branch and both reviews preserved.\n- Goal: the note and document editors become rich markdown editors, Obsidian-style — syntax marks hide except around the caret.\n- Key ruling: the markdown SOURCE stays the document model; editors with their own model that serialize back (ProseMirror, TipTap, Lexical, Milkdown) are ruled out — round-trips rewrite bytes the user never touched and break verbatim storage.\n- Stack: ink-mde (CodeMirror 6, Solid component) first choice; fallback @codemirror/lang-markdown + ixora. Hand-written code is glue only: the #tag pill widget, autosave, theming, prefs toggle.\n- Autosave replaces Save/Cancel: debounced ~500ms plus flush on blur; every write conditional (`was`) so a concurrent agent edit refuses loudly instead of clobbering.\n- Ship the note editor first, then the document editor. Vim mode via @replit/codemirror-vim, off by default, in prefs.","created":"2026-08-18T11:16:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:02:45-04:00","custom":{"parked":"2026-08-18 by the human's ruling (\"unhappy with markdown editor, revisit in distant future\") — draft PR #241 holds the work, branch + both reviews preserved, ten evidence images on the attachments CDN"}}
{"id":"hindsight-comparison","parent":"sd-mcp","ord":"a0","title":"Olai vs Hindsight: which agent-memory features are worth adopting #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- Comparison against hindsight.vectorize.io, keeping files as the single source of truth. Brainstorm: docs/brainstorming/hindsight.md.\n- Six recommendations: semantic search as a derived gitignored index; time/graph recall as query clauses; capture-as-proposal at conversation end; consolidation as a stale/duplicates reading; per-connection scoping for multiple agents; sync stays git.\n- Deliberately not copied: LLM-normalized notes, identity config, hosted memory.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-08-21T14:45:40-04:00"}
